---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — William Montoya"
  description="I'm William Montoya. A UX designer, journalist, and teacher from Medellín designing at the intersection of systems, education, and human possibility."
  ogImage="https://dejesumensaje.com/assets/william-montoya.jpg"
  ogType="website"
  themeColor="#1a1a1a"
  bodyClass="about-page"
  footerBridge={false}
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/about-story.css" />
    <script type="application/ld+json" is:inline>{JSON.stringify({
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "ProfilePage",
      "mainEntity": {
        "@type": "Person",
        "name": "William Montoya",
        "jobTitle": "Senior Product Designer",
        "url": "https://dejesumensaje.com/about.html",
        "sameAs": [
          "https://www.linkedin.com/in/dejesumensaje/",
          "https://medium.com/@dejesumensaje",
          "https://github.com/Dejesumensaje"
        ]
      }
    })}</script>
  </Fragment>

  <main id="main-content">

    <!-- 01 — IDENTITY -->
    <section class="about-hero" data-bg="var(--color-text)" aria-labelledby="about-heading">
      <div class="about-hero__photo">
        <picture>
          <source srcset="/assets/william-montoya.webp" type="image/webp" />
          <img src="/assets/william-montoya.jpg" width="1000" height="750" alt="William Montoya" />
        </picture>
      </div>
      <div class="about-hero__content">
        <span class="about-eyebrow">Senior Product Designer · Medellín</span>
        <h1 id="about-heading" class="about-name">William <br>Montoya.</h1>
        <p class="about-tagline">Designing at the intersection of systems, <br>education, and human possibility.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 — STORY + EXPERIENCE -->
    <section class="about-story" data-bg="var(--canvas)">
      <div class="about-story__inner">

        <blockquote class="about-pull">
          I began as a journalist, trying to understand how information shapes people.
        </blockquote>

        <div class="about-story__body">
          <p>That search brought me to Colombia's Ministry of Education, where I helped redesign national platforms used by teachers, students, and families across the country. Working there transformed my understanding of design: it's not just about usability, it's about creating access, strengthening public capacity, and building tools that expand opportunity. That sense of purpose has guided my work ever since.</p>
          <p>I see information architecture as the craft of giving shape to meaning. I work to simplify complexity without diluting what matters. I design from the system outward, not the surface inward. Writing is central to my process because it forces clarity. Research helps me dismantle assumptions. Iteration keeps me honest.</p>
          <p>Design should create understanding. It should respect people's intelligence, time, and context. It should reach those who usually get overlooked. Whether I'm designing for education or enterprise platforms — those commitments shape the decisions I make.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="about-snapshot">
          <div class="snapshot-item">
            <span class="snapshot-label">Currently</span>
            <p>Embedded with Deloitte through Globant, working across product, UX, and information architecture.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="snapshot-item">
            <span class="snapshot-label">Focus</span>
            <p>Complex service flows, content-heavy ecosystems, and interfaces that need clearer structure.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="snapshot-item">
            <span class="snapshot-label">Strengths</span>
            <p>Turning research, systems thinking, and design direction into decisions teams can actually build.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-story__xp">
          <span class="section-label">Experience</span>
          <div class="xp-grid">

            <div class="xp-item">
              <span class="xp-year">2023 — Now</span>
              <span class="xp-company">Globant / Deloitte</span>
              <span class="xp-role">Senior Product Designer</span>
              <p class="xp-note">Design systems, pricing tools, and AI governance for Converge for Restaurants (KFC, Pizza Hut).</p>
            </div>

            <div class="xp-item">
              <span class="xp-year">2022 — 2023</span>
              <span class="xp-company">Globant / CashPak</span>
              <span class="xp-role">UX Designer</span>
              <!-- TODO(William): one-line impact, e.g.
              <p class="xp-note">Designed X for Y, improving Z.</p>
              -->
            </div>

            <div class="xp-item">
              <span class="xp-year">2021 — 2022</span>
              <span class="xp-company">Globant / Blackboard</span>
              <span class="xp-role">Product Designer</span>
              <!-- TODO(William): one-line impact, e.g.
              <p class="xp-note">Designed X for Y, improving Z.</p>
              -->
            </div>

            <div class="xp-item">
              <span class="xp-year">2019 — 2021</span>
              <span class="xp-company">Ministry of Education</span>
              <span class="xp-role">UX Lead</span>
              <p class="xp-note">Led the redesign of Colombia Aprende and Aprender Digital — national platforms serving millions of teachers and students.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="xp-item">
              <span class="xp-year">2017 — 2018</span>
              <span class="xp-company">UNDP</span>
              <span class="xp-role">Product Designer</span>
              <!-- TODO(William): one-line impact, e.g.
              <p class="xp-note">Designed X for Y, improving Z.</p>
              -->
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 — CRAFT + BEYOND -->
    <section class="about-craft" data-bg="var(--color-surface)">
      <div class="about-craft__inner">

        <h2 class="craft-heading">Craft</h2>

        <div class="craft-groups">
          <div class="craft-group">
            <p class="craft-group-label">UX Core</p>
            <div class="craft-tags">
              <span class="tag">User Research</span>
              <span class="tag">Information Architecture</span>
              <span class="tag">Usability Testing</span>
              <span class="tag">UX Writing</span>
              <span class="tag">Wireframing</span>
              <span class="tag">Prototyping</span>
              <span class="tag">Design Strategy</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="craft-group">
            <p class="craft-group-label">Tools</p>
            <div class="craft-tags">
              <span class="tag">Figma</span>
              <span class="tag">Notion</span>
              <span class="tag">Miro</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="craft-group">
            <p class="craft-group-label">Strengths</p>
            <div class="craft-tags">
              <span class="tag">Accessibility</span>
              <span class="tag">Design Systems</span>
              <span class="tag">Workshop Facilitation</span>
              <span class="tag">AI-assisted workflows</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-workflow">
          <h3 class="workflow-heading">How I work today</h3>
          <div class="workflow-items">

            <div class="workflow-item">
              <span class="workflow-tool">Claude</span>
              <p>I use Claude as a thinking partner throughout the design process — not to generate answers, but to sharpen questions. Research synthesis, writing structure, edge-case mapping, stakeholder argument preparation. It extends the thinking, never replaces it.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="workflow-item">
              <span class="workflow-tool">Figma + Figma Make</span>
              <p>Figma is where I design. Figma Make is where I prototype at speed — full interaction coverage, every state, before the first stakeholder review. The AI executes the iterations; the design decisions are mine.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="workflow-item">
              <span class="workflow-tool">Notion</span>
              <p>Documentation, research synthesis, and project tracking all live in Notion. I write to think — before meetings, after research sessions, and whenever a design decision needs a clear rationale that will survive the room.</p>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="about-beyond">
          <h3 class="beyond-heading">Beyond design</h3>
          <div class="beyond-strips">

            <div class="beyond-strip">
              <div class="beyond-label">
                <span class="beyond-num">01</span>
                <p class="beyond-title">Teaching</p>
              </div>
              <div class="beyond-body">
                <p>I teach sensory thinking at Universidad de Antioquia — exploring how perception, emotion, and attention shape the way people experience digital systems.</p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="beyond-strip">
              <div class="beyond-label">
                <span class="beyond-num">02</span>
                <p class="beyond-title">Alucine</p>
              </div>
              <div class="beyond-body">
                <p>I run Alucine, a project about film and culture. It's where I explore stories, symbols, and the ways narrative can shift how we understand the world.</p>
                <a href="https://alucine.co/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="beyond-link">alucine.co ↗</a>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="beyond-strip">
              <div class="beyond-label">
                <span class="beyond-num">03</span>
                <p class="beyond-title">Games &amp; Tools</p>
              </div>
              <div class="beyond-body">
                <p>Videogames taught me about systems, choice, and feedback loops. AI is now a regular part of how I design — accelerating iteration, not replacing judgment.</p>
                <a href="https://backloggd.com/u/dejesumensaje/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="beyond-link">backloggd ↗</a>
              </div>
            </div>

          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

  </main>

</BaseLayout>
